I like the Fedora for the archeologist character, but it's a pity that
it isn't really worth keeping, and most players would quickly trade it
for a better helmet. Indy, on the other hand, was quite attached to
his hat and always went back for it. I was wondering whether there
might be some advantage it could bestow which might make other
archaeologists feel likewise.

The most fitting thing, afaics, is to make wearing a fedora give you
some small luck bonus, like a lesser luckstone. That would certainly
seem to characterise the Indiana-Jones-style archaeologist quite well.
What do people think?

